    "exact_target": "Does every elliptic curve in the specified number-field class occur in the automorphic cohomology predicted by Thorne's modularity formulation?",
    "definition_tex": "\\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}\nFor $E/K$ with $\\operatorname{End}_K(E)={\\mathbb{Z}}$, let $(r_v,N_v)$ be its finite-place Weil--Deligne representations. Use Thorne's geometric-Frobenius convention to form\n\\[\n \\pi(E)=\\bigotimes_{v\\nmid\\infty}'\n \\operatorname{rec}_{K_v}^{-1}(r_v\\otimes|\\cdot|^{1/2},N_v),\\qquad\n A=\\varinjlim_U H^*(Y_U,{\\mathbb{Q}}).\n\\]\nHere $Y_U$ are the adelic locally symmetric spaces in the source, and the transition maps give the finite-adelic group action. The assertion is the existence of a $\\operatorname{GL}_2({\\mathbb{A}}_K^\\infty)$-equivariant injection $\\pi(E)\\hookrightarrow A\\otimes_{{\\mathbb{Q}}}{\\mathbb{C}}$. The condition concerns endomorphisms \\emph{over $K$}; replacing it by $\\operatorname{End}_{\\bar K}(E)={\\mathbb{Z}}$ would narrow the target.\n\\par\\smallskip\\textit{Formulation and concept references:} \\href{https://ems.press/content/book-chapter-files/28276}{[S1]}.\n\n\\subsection{Short English statement}\nDoes every elliptic curve in the specified number-field class occur in the automorphic cohomology predicted by Thorne's modularity formulation?\n\n\\subsection{Sources}\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item[S1]J. A. Thorne, Elliptic curves and modularity, 8ECM proceedings, EMS Press, 2023, DOI 10.4171/8ECM/12.\n\\url{https://ems.press/content/book-chapter-files/28276}.\n\\textit{Formulation source.}\n\\item[S2]Elliptic curves and modularity.\n\\url{https://ems.press/content/book-chapter-files/28276?nt=1}.\n\\textit{Further reference; not a proof endorsement.}\n\\item[S3]Modularity of elliptic curves over cyclotomic Z\\_p-extensions of real quadratic fields.\n\\url{https://arxiv.org/html/2206.12860v1}.\n\\textit{Further reference; not a proof endorsement.}\n\\item[S4]Modular elliptic curves and hyperbolic uniformization.\n\\url{https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.03830}.\n\\textit{Further reference; not a proof endorsement.}\n\\end{itemize}",
