    "exact_target": "Must entanglement in every uniformly gapped two-dimensional local ground state grow at most in proportion to a region's boundary?",
    "definition_tex": "\\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}\nLet $H_\\Lambda$ be a finite-range bounded Hamiltonian on a finite square-lattice region, with fixed finite site dimension, unique normalized ground state $|\\psi_\\Lambda\\rangle$, and spectral gap at least $\\Delta>0$ uniformly in $\\Lambda$. For $A\\subseteq\\Lambda$, put\n\\[\n \\rho_A=\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\Lambda\\setminus A}|\\psi_\\Lambda\\rangle\\langle\\psi_\\Lambda|,\n \\qquad S(\\rho_A)=-\\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho_A\\log\\rho_A).\n\\]\nThe conjecture is $S(\\rho_A)\\le C|\\partial A|$, where $|\\partial A|$ counts lattice edges crossing to the complement. The constant may depend on the fixed interaction parameters and gap but not on the region or system size.\n\\par\\smallskip\\textit{Formulation and concept references:} \\href{https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00220-026-05554-z}{[S1]}.\n\n\\subsection{Short English statement}\nMust entanglement in every uniformly gapped two-dimensional local ground state grow at most in proportion to a region's boundary?\n\n\\subsection{Sources}\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item[S1]I. Arad, R. Firanko, R. Jain, Area Laws and Tensor Networks for Maximally Mixed Ground States, Communications in Mathematical Physics 407, 54 (2026).\n\\url{https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00220-026-05554-z}.\n\\textit{Formulation source.}\n\\item[S2]Universal lower bound on topological entanglement entropy.\n\\url{https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.00689}.\n\\textit{Further reference; not a proof endorsement.}\n\\end{itemize}",
