    "exact_target": "Can every finite set with small additive doubling in any abelian group be covered efficiently by translates of a low-dimensional convex coset progression?",
    "definition_tex": "\\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}\nFor a nonempty finite set $A$ in an abelian group, define $A+A=\\{a+a':a,a'\\in A\\}$ and suppose $|A+A|\\le K|A|$, $K\\ge1$. A centered convex coset progression of dimension $d$ has the form\n$P=H+\\phi(C\\cap{\\mathbb{Z}}^d)$, where $H$ is a finite subgroup, $\\phi:{\\mathbb{Z}}^d\\to G$ is a homomorphism, and $C\\subset{\\mathbb{R}}^d$ is a centrally symmetric convex body centered at zero. The assertion is that an absolute $C_0$ allows\n\\[\n A\\subseteq\\bigcup_{t\\in T}(t+P),\\quad |T|\\le K^{C_0},\n \\quad d\\le C_0\\log K,\\quad |P|\\le K^{C_0}|A|.\n\\]\nNo bounded exponent or torsion-free restriction is placed on the ambient group, and the selected progression is convex rather than necessarily rectangular.\n\\par\\smallskip\\textit{Formulation and concept references:} \\href{https://www.ams.org/journals/bull/2013-50-01/S0273-0979-2012-01392-7/S0273-0979-2012-01392-7.pdf}{[S1]}.\n\n\\subsection{Short English statement}\nCan every finite set with small additive doubling in any abelian group be covered efficiently by translates of a low-dimensional convex coset progression?\n\n\\subsection{Sources}\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item[S1]Tom Sanders, \"The structure theory of set addition revisited,\" Bulletin (New Series) of the American Mathematical Society, Volume 50, Number 1, January 2013, Pages 93-127; S 0273-0979(2012)01392-7, published electronically October 2, 2012.\n\\url{https://www.ams.org/journals/bull/2013-50-01/S0273-0979-2012-01392-7/S0273-0979-2012-01392-7.pdf}.\n\\textit{Formulation source.}\n\\end{itemize}",
    "definition_file": "attacks/open_problems/top_problems/30006785.tex",
    "link": null,
    "external_url": null,
    "sources": [
      {
        "citation": "Tom Sanders, \"The structure theory of set addition revisited,\" Bulletin (New Series) of the American Mathematical Society, Volume 50, Number 1, January 2013, Pages 93-127; S 0273-0979(2012)01392-7, published electronically October 2, 2012.",
        "url": "https://www.ams.org/journals/bull/2013-50-01/S0273-0979-2012-01392-7/S0273-0979-2012-01392-7.pdf"
      }
    ],
    "status": "open",
