    "exact_target": "Must every endomorphism of the one-variable Weyl algebra over a characteristic-zero field be invertible?",
    "definition_tex": "\\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}\nFor a characteristic-zero field $K$, the first Weyl algebra is\n\\[\n A_1(K)=K\\langle x,\\partial\\rangle/(\\partial x-x\\partial-1),\n\\]\nthe associative algebra of polynomial differential operators in one variable. The selected Dixmier conjecture asks whether every unital $K$-algebra homomorphism $\\phi:A_1(K)\\to A_1(K)$ is bijective, and hence an automorphism. An endomorphism is specified by a pair $P=\\phi(x)$, $Q=\\phi(\\partial)$ satisfying $QP-PQ=1$; the assertion is that such a pair generates all of $A_1(K)$ and yields an invertible substitution. This entry is specifically the first Weyl algebra in characteristic zero. The proof-claim title in the supplied bibliography is not treated as proof of this assertion.\n\\par\\smallskip\\textit{Formulation and concept references:} \\href{https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.06959}{[S1]}.\n\n\\subsection{Short English statement}\nMust every endomorphism of the one-variable Weyl algebra over a characteristic-zero field be invertible?\n\n\\subsection{Sources}\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item[S1]Alexander Zheglov, The Conjecture of Dixmier for the first Weyl algebra is true, arXiv:2410.06959v5, 2026.\n\\url{https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.06959}.\n\\textit{Formulation source.}\n\\end{itemize}",
    "definition_file": "attacks/open_problems/top_problems/30006868.tex",
    "link": null,
    "external_url": null,
    "sources": [
      {
        "citation": "Alexander Zheglov, The Conjecture of Dixmier for the first Weyl algebra is true, arXiv:2410.06959v5, 2026.",
        "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.06959"
      }
    ],
    "status": "open",
